From 795b006d4afb17228d837a984a3921e3a8b225e6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Connor Baker <ConnorBaker01@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 19:52:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] [Operators] Import torch only where the blockscaled GEMM
 kernels need it

nvidia-cutlass-operators makes torch an optional dependency (the "torch"
extra), and the operators package checks is_torch_available() before
importing it. But importing cutlass.operators loads the CuTe DSL GEMM
provider, which imports the sm107 dense blockscaled GEMM kernels, and their
modules import torch and cutlass.torch unconditionally. Without torch,
`import cutlass.operators` fails with "CuTeDSLProvider is unavailable".

Only the reference implementations and the test harness in these modules use
torch, not the kernels, so import torch and cutlass.torch only when torch is
installed, as find_spec, which is_torch_available() uses, reports. Quote the
torch.Tensor annotations of those helpers, which are evaluated when the
functions are defined.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
